   $q$The author says early riders were "wary" of elevators. Which word is closest in meaning to "wary" as used here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bored","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-context"},{"text":"Excited","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Cautious","is_correct":true},{"text":"Angry","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-extreme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Cautious$q$, $q$The next sentences explain that a snapped rope could send the platform "straight down the shaft," so riders were cautious. "Angry" goes too far; nothing suggests people were furious, only careful.$q$, 'draft', '2462c730-093c-517d-8801-94b1d288a8d5')
