  ('3eec6d11-360e-548f-a962-af21744e0d95', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author says the best safety inventions "have quietly done their job." What is the role of the word "quietly" in the final paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that modern elevators make much less noise than old ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It supports the idea that success means working so reliably that no one notices.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It criticizes passengers for not thanking the inventors of the brake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It suggests that safety inventions are often kept secret from riders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It supports the idea that success means working so reliably that no one notices.$q$, $q$"Quietly" personifies the inventions as modest workers, which supports the claim that people "rarely give them a second thought" because the devices succeed. The passage says nothing about noise levels, so the literal reading misses the point.$q$, 'draft', '2462c730-093c-517d-8801-94b1d288a8d5')
