values
  ('4bc17117-d1d5-5dce-869d-39c1d3dfad15', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author concludes that cheerful language "is not the enemy. It is simply a clue." What is the role of this contrast in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests that buyers should write cheerful listings of their own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"It tells buyers to ignore listings completely and shop only in stores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It argues that sellers who use euphemisms should be reported for lying.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shifts the reader from distrusting euphemisms to using them as signals to inspect closely.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shifts the reader from distrusting euphemisms to using them as signals to inspect closely.$q$, $q$Calling the language "a clue" rather than "the enemy" reframes euphemisms as hints, and the last sentence says a buyer "should work just as hard to look closely." The author says the language is "not exactly dishonest," so reporting sellers for lying contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '5881a7d5-59e2-52c6-94a7-1ea9049b07d8')
