values
  ('dc436ce9-6724-563b-8da2-d09786907863', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The author explains why scientists call the plants "thrifty" rather than "stingy." What is the key difference between the two words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Thrifty\" means storing water, while \"stingy\" means storing food.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-denotation"},{"text":"\"Thrifty\" means wasteful, while \"stingy\" means careful with resources.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-connotation"},{"text":"\"Stingy\" is the more scientific word, while \"thrifty\" is casual.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Both describe saving, but \"thrifty\" sounds wise while \"stingy\" sounds selfish.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both describe saving, but "thrifty" sounds wise while "stingy" sounds selfish.$q$, $q$The passage says a thrifty plant "uses its resources wisely," while "stingy" suggests "selfishness, as if the plant were refusing to share." Both words share the idea of saving, so the difference is connotation, not what is being saved.$q$, 'draft', 'e7e59545-576f-5455-8b37-f3bcf51196e8')
