values
  ('684636ca-af9a-52c2-a0e5-94fb6161bf5f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The clear patch on each leaf is described as "a kind of window." What does this metaphor help the reader understand?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The patch lets animals look inside the plant to find water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"The patch is made of glass that the plant takes from the sand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The patch lets light pass through to the hidden parts of the plant.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The patch can be opened and closed like the window of a house.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The patch lets light pass through to the hidden parts of the plant.$q$, $q$Like a window, the patch "lets light pass down into the buried tissue." The comparison is about letting light through, not about opening and closing, which the passage never mentions.$q$, 'draft', 'e7e59545-576f-5455-8b37-f3bcf51196e8')
