   $q$The sentence "The letters grew shorter as the bridge grew longer" mainly helps to:$q$, $q$[{"text":"compress a long stretch of time into one line while hinting at the writer's growing tiredness.","is_correct":true},{"text":"show that the archive is missing several letters from the middle of the box.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"explain the engineering reasons the bridge took several years to build.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"introduce a flashback to the writer's childhood before he worked on bridges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$compress a long stretch of time into one line while hinting at the writer's growing tiredness.$q$, $q$The parallel phrasing summarizes a long stretch of time quickly and links shrinking letters to the demanding work. There is no flashback and no hint of missing letters.$q$, 'draft', 'ed175c7e-8e4b-554a-986e-8657ca6d97cf')
