   $q$What cultural experience does the speaker describe in this poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Learning Vietnamese for the first time in a high school language class","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Interpreting between a parent and an English speaker as the child of immigrants","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teaching a parent to drive so the family can travel on Sundays","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Working at a counter and helping customers fill out their papers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-narrator"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Interpreting between a parent and an English speaker as the child of immigrants$q$, $q$The speaker turns the clerk's words "into Vietnamese" for the father and carries his answers "back in English." The car keys are a comparison, not a driving lesson.$q$, 'draft', 'ba38fac0-98d2-578f-91aa-780c67c15e31')
