   $q$How does the author show the passage of time in the fourth paragraph to emphasize the heron's problem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The paragraph slows down to describe a single minute of the flood in great detail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing"},{"text":"The paragraph jumps back to the heron's childhood to explain why she liked calendars.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The paragraph skips forward several years to show the heron as an old bird.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Specific dates from her plan are set against the flood's changes, showing her schedule falling apart.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Specific dates from her plan are set against the flood's changes, showing her schedule falling apart.$q$, $q$Dates from her plan, like the fourth and the fifteenth, collide with the flood's events, such as the north bank going underwater on the third, so time is measured by what breaks. There is no flashback or leap of years.$q$, 'draft', 'cf39a7c7-5f49-5b95-86ec-fb50ce48488b')
