   $q$Which sentence should be left out of an objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kits bundled the design, materials and instructions into a single purchase.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-fact-for-opinion"},{"text":"The business faded as more towns gained lumberyards and trained builders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-fact-for-opinion"},{"text":"The kit companies cared more about their profits than about the families who bought from them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Hundreds of kit houses still stand in Vellin County today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-fact-for-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The kit companies cared more about their profits than about the families who bought from them.$q$, $q$An objective summary reports what the text says without adding judgments, and the passage never makes a claim about the companies' motives. The other three sentences restate facts from paragraphs 2, 4 and 3.$q$, 'draft', '800edc91-6bef-5e00-aa9d-08739653e7d0')
