   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Port Sabelle built a new aquatic center with gutters along every wall. The designer, Kwame Ostrander, made the pool deeper than the old pool, and the city's coaches noticed the difference quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Swimmers' strokes create waves that slow racers. Spinning lane lines, edge gutters and greater depth reduce those waves, and in Port Sabelle outer lane times moved closer to middle lane times. Design cannot replace training, but it makes races fairer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Swimmers lose races because of waves, not training. Every city should rebuild its pool the way Port Sabelle did, since a well-designed pool is the real secret to winning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Swimmers create waves when they race, and those waves bounce off walls. Because of this, swimming is one of the hardest sports to judge fairly, and many results are not accurate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Swimmers' strokes create waves that slow racers. Spinning lane lines, edge gutters and greater depth reduce those waves, and in Port Sabelle outer lane times moved closer to middle lane times. Design cannot replace training, but it makes races fairer.$q$, $q$The summary beginning "Swimmers' strokes create waves" includes the problem, the solutions, the evidence and the final qualification without adding opinions. The summary beginning "Port Sabelle built a new aquatic center" is accurate but covers only details from paragraphs 3 and 4.$q$, 'draft', '79e6575b-848f-55d7-8f2a-eb00e44be484')
