   $q$Which evidence best supports the inference that Femi started the race much too fast?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Femi is a freshman running in his very first varsity meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"Keanu, though slower than his usual pace, is catching Femi before the climb.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coach Brandt tells the whole team to run their own race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Femi lies on the grass with his arms over his face after finishing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keanu, though slower than his usual pace, is catching Femi before the climb.$q$, $q$Keanu is eleven seconds slower than usual, yet the "orange shirt was getting larger," so Femi must be slowing sharply after an early sprint. Being a freshman or lying on the grass afterward fits many situations and does not prove his pace was too fast.$q$, 'draft', '1f875b6b-f212-5b67-9fe0-7406cdfa38d6')
