   $q$Which inference about Coach Brandt is best supported by the end of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He is angry that Keanu ignored his instruction and plans to punish him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"He has not noticed that Keanu and Femi finished side by side.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He is disappointed in Femi for slowing down his more experienced teammate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He quietly approves of what Keanu did, even though it broke his instruction.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He quietly approves of what Keanu did, even though it broke his instruction.$q$, $q$The coach looks at Keanu "for longer than he needed to," and his mouth moves in a way that is "not quite a frown," which hints at approval he does not say aloud. His remark names the broken instruction, but those details show he is not truly angry.$q$, 'draft', '1f875b6b-f212-5b67-9fe0-7406cdfa38d6')
