   $q$According to the poem, what does Mr. Haddad do at the hill by the clinic?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He spreads extra salt before he turns around.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"He lowers the plow blade a little farther.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He stops to wave at the nurses arriving for work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He writes the hill in his log as a special stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He lowers the plow blade a little farther.$q$, $q$The second stanza says that at the clinic hill "he lowers the blade a little farther." He does not wave (nobody is awake), and the last stanza says he does not write the hill down.$q$, 'draft', 'f3466347-0c3a-58a9-85ea-589f2924bad5')
