   $q$The children talk "as if the streets had cleared themselves at dawn." What does this detail suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The snow melted on its own before the buses left the depot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The children do not realize anyone worked through the night to clear the roads.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The children know Mr. Haddad and are joking about his job.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The children are glad that school has been canceled for the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The children do not realize anyone worked through the night to clear the roads.$q$, $q$"As if" signals that the streets did not really clear themselves; the children simply never see the plow, since "Nobody is awake to wave." The buses are running, so school has not been canceled.$q$, 'draft', 'f3466347-0c3a-58a9-85ea-589f2924bad5')
