   $q$The poem says, "There is no line on the form for the clinic hill, / so he does not write it down." What does this most strongly suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He is hiding a mistake he made while plowing the clinic hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"His extra care goes unrecorded, and he does it without needing credit.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He is careless with paperwork and often leaves his log unfinished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"He forgot about the clinic hill by the time he returned to the depot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His extra care goes unrecorded, and he does it without needing credit.$q$, $q$The log records only "miles driven, salt used, time returned," so the extra effort at the clinic leaves no trace, and he accepts that, just as no one wakes to thank him. He fills in every listed field, so the lines do not show carelessness.$q$, 'draft', 'f3466347-0c3a-58a9-85ea-589f2924bad5')
