   $q$Which detail from Hester's letter explains why she kept the readings that summer?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her father had been \"laid up with his leg all summer.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"She was writing to her aunt in the month of August.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"She was \"more particular\" about the readings than he was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"She had \"taken over the readings\" for the family farm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-not-explains"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her father had been "laid up with his leg all summer."$q$, $q$Hester says her father was laid up, "so" she took over, which gives the cause. Being "more particular" describes how she kept the readings, not why she started keeping them.$q$, 'draft', '159dae90-fd07-5b66-9a26-5393df1ab587')
