   $q$What do the sign's letters, once gold and now "the color of tea," suggest about the shop?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The shop is about to close because business has dried up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"The shop also sells tea and baked goods to its customers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The grandfather recently painted the sign a new brown color.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It has been there a long time without its sign being renewed.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It has been there a long time without its sign being renewed.$q$, $q$Letters that were gold "before I was born" and have since faded to the color of tea show age and wear over many years. Faded paint alone does not show the shop is about to close; the grandfather still opens each morning.$q$, 'draft', '37d0465c-8de8-515d-8f30-327b0ed629e5')
