   $q$What can be inferred from the grandfather's answer about buying a new machine?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He believes his old machine sews better than a new one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He cannot afford to buy a newer sewing machine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He is annoyed that the speaker interrupted his work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He has never seen how a modern machine performs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He believes his old machine sews better than a new one.$q$, $q$He shows seams "as even as a ruler" and challenges, "Find me a new one that can do this," meaning he trusts the old machine's quality. The poem never mentions money, so cost is not supported.$q$, 'draft', '37d0465c-8de8-515d-8f30-327b0ed629e5')
