-- Passage rg10-story-details-inference-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0ba977b6-b0ef-5ef9-9e77-8f888d269a25', 'rg10-story-details-inference-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-story-details-inference'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Out of Time$q$, $q$The final round of the regional chess tournament was played in a school cafeteria that still smelled faintly of pizza. Mei Abara sat across from a boy named Lorenzo who had beaten her twice last year, both times in fewer than thirty moves. He wore a green hoodie and tapped the clock with one finger, never his whole hand.

Mei's older brother, Tunde, was not allowed in the playing area, so he watched from the doorway, where he could see only the back of her head. He had taught her to play when she was six, on a board with two missing pawns replaced by bottle caps. She had beaten him for the first time at nine, and he had not played her since.

The game went long. By move forty, most of the other boards were empty, and a small crowd of parents and players had gathered around theirs. Lorenzo had an extra pawn, and Mei had twelve minutes left on her clock to his four. She did not hurry. Twice she reached toward a piece, stopped, and folded her hands in her lap instead.

On move fifty-one Lorenzo offered a draw. Mei looked at the board for a full minute. Then she shook her head and moved her king one square to the left.

Six moves later, Lorenzo's clock ran out. The tournament director stopped it and wrote the result on the sheet. Lorenzo stared at the board, then reached across and shook Mei's hand without a word, and left so quickly that he forgot his water bottle.

Mei found her brother in the hallway. He was holding her coat, and he was smiling in a way she had not seen in a while.

"You should have taken the draw," he said. "You were worse."

"I know," she said. "But he was out of time, and I wasn't."

Tunde handed her the coat. On the drive home he asked if she still had the old board with the bottle caps, and when she said yes, he asked if she would set it up after dinner.$q$, 'draft')
