   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A runner on the curve drops the baton, but Marisol picks it up and still wins the race for the team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"A relay runner describes running the unwatched curve, handing off to the anchor who gets the attention, and keeping a photo anyway.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A runner takes the baton from a teammate named Dev while it is still warm from his hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"An underappreciated runner bravely carries the whole team while a selfish teammate steals the glory.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A relay runner describes running the unwatched curve, handing off to the anchor who gets the attention, and keeping a photo anyway.$q$, $q$The correct summary follows the poem from the curve to the handoff to the photo without judging anyone. Calling Marisol selfish adds an opinion the poem never states.$q$, 'draft', '867c859c-b4a3-5d8e-928b-72a4870b9830')
