   $q$How do the final two lines of the poem shape its theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They reveal that the team lost the race even though the speaker ran that leg of the relay well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They suggest that the speaker plans to ask the coach for the final leg of the relay next season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They move the speaker's focus from who is seen in the photo to the fact that the baton arrived, showing the speaker values the shared result.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They reveal the speaker's bitterness that only Marisol is clearly shown in the photo on the school website.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They move the speaker's focus from who is seen in the photo to the fact that the baton arrived, showing the speaker values the shared result.$q$, $q$After admitting to being only "a shape behind her shoulder," the speaker keeps the photo because it shows the baton "got there," finding worth in the team's result. "Anyway" signals acceptance, not bitterness.$q$, 'draft', '867c859c-b4a3-5d8e-928b-72a4870b9830')
