   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Short, efficient answers always make the best impression in formal meetings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Running a small bakery requires early mornings and loyal regular customers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Speaking for someone else means carrying their full voice, not making it smaller.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Children who translate for their parents should be paid for their important work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Speaking for someone else means carrying their full voice, not making it smaller.$q$, $q$Mateo's short version fails to reach Ms. Halvorsen, and he realizes he has been shrinking his father by editing him. The bakery choice lists details of the topic, not the lesson the story develops.$q$, 'draft', '449bc0cf-0735-56ec-90ec-03e29a31c04d')
