   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mateo rudely ignores his hardworking father at the bank, which is a shameful way for any son to treat a parent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Mateo's father describes a recipe for conchas that his own father once wrote on the back of a calendar page.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"At a bank meeting, Mateo shortens his father's long answer, his father asks him to translate every word, and Mateo realizes he has been shrinking his father's voice.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ms. Halvorsen approves the loan on the spot, and the bakery buys a second oven by the end of the week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At a bank meeting, Mateo shortens his father's long answer, his father asks him to translate every word, and Mateo realizes he has been shrinking his father's voice.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the shortened answer, the father's request, and Mateo's realization in neutral language. The loan is never approved in the passage; she only says she will call within a week.$q$, 'draft', '449bc0cf-0735-56ec-90ec-03e29a31c04d')
