   $q$The Latin root fid means "faith" or "trust." What does Mr. Szabo mean by "Fidelity to the original"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Staying exactly true to what the letter says","is_correct":true},{"text":"Keeping the original letters locked away safely","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Reading each letter aloud before copying it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Fixing every error so the letter reads well","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Staying exactly true to what the letter says$q$, $q$Fidelity means faithfulness, and Mr. Szabo explains it as "Copy exactly what you see," even misspellings. Fixing errors is exactly what he tells Priya not to do.$q$, 'draft', 'edfad48f-1897-5b29-a6df-497e5fa046bb')
