   $q$The Latin root ped means "foot." What is a "pedestrian bridge"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A bridge built only for railroad workers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A bridge built for people traveling on foot","is_correct":true},{"text":"A bridge built for heavy freight trains","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A bridge built mainly for delivery trucks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A bridge built for people traveling on foot$q$, $q$Ped means "foot," and the bridge carries "walkers and cyclists over the tracks." The freight trains run underneath the bridge, not across it.$q$, 'draft', '561426fe-8037-5ada-8121-ba0a8b7ad0a4')
