  ('45999f6a-ff6c-57d1-88cb-f63450b924a6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The Latin root sequ means "follow." What does "a strict sequence" mean in the third paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A firm deadline for finishing the whole bridge","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-idea"},{"text":"A fixed order in which each step follows another","is_correct":true},{"text":"A careful list of the workers on each crew","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A strict rule about how fast cranes may move","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A fixed order in which each step follows another$q$, $q$A sequence is an order where one thing follows another, shown by "towers first, then the span, then railings and lights." A deadline is about when work ends, not the order of steps.$q$, 'draft', '561426fe-8037-5ada-8121-ba0a8b7ad0a4')
