   $q$The prefix sub- can mean "next" or "after," and sequ means "follow." What is "the subsequent school year"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The school year before the bridge was approved","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-frame"},{"text":"The school year that came after the bridge opened","is_correct":true},{"text":"A school year that was shorter than usual","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-prefix"},{"text":"The school year when the bridge was being built","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The school year that came after the bridge opened$q$, $q$Subsequent means "following after," and the paragraph describes results after the bridge opened, such as students arriving on time. A year before the approval would come earlier, not after.$q$, 'draft', '561426fe-8037-5ada-8121-ba0a8b7ad0a4')
