  ('955fcb4a-6da2-5453-a590-5187fd971cb7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The root ver means "true," and dict means "say," so a verdict was first a "true saying" in a courtroom. What does "the best verdict" mean in the last sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The apology the district sent to the newspaper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The official ruling of a judge in a court case","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"The most favorable judgment of her work she could get","is_correct":true},{"text":"The final number printed in the corrected article","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The most favorable judgment of her work she could get$q$, $q$Here verdict is used broadly to mean an opinion or judgment, and it refers to Wen's praise of her rewritten article. No court appears in the story, so the courtroom meaning is too literal for this context.$q$, 'draft', '5a67b95b-ebcb-5bb8-9b9d-986e52e1e701')
