   $q$The prefix con- means "together" or "with," and duc means "lead." What does "conduct water from mountain springs" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Guide water along a path from the springs","is_correct":true},{"text":"Behave properly near the mountain springs","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-sense"},{"text":"Measure how clean the spring water is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Block water from leaving the springs","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Guide water along a path from the springs$q$, $q$Here conduct is a verb meaning "lead" or "carry," since the water travels from the springs "to the highest terraces." Conduct can also mean behavior, but that sense makes no sense with water as the object.$q$, 'draft', '1c3ac066-7dd6-5e4a-94b3-da82b7156735')
