   $q$How does the author respond to the objection that the requirement would burden property owners?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By claiming that most property owners already support the requirement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"By arguing the coating is cheap, pays for itself and could be aided by grants.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By pointing out that flat roofs cannot be seen from the sidewalk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaims"},{"text":"By admitting the burden is large but arguing that public safety outweighs it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By arguing the coating is cheap, pays for itself and could be aided by grants.$q$, $q$The fourth paragraph says a coating costs far less than a new roof, cooling savings "would repay most owners within a few summers," and grants could help. The sidewalk point answers a different objection, about appearance.$q$, 'draft', 'd9176f60-6879-5e74-bee5-83307ea28e8d')
