   $q$What does the anecdote about the speaker's early program contribute to the speech?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By blaming the team that inherited it, the speaker shows that other programmers often lack the skill to read good code.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-anecdote"},{"text":"By describing that fast program, the speaker proves that compact code is usually better than code with long explanations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"By admitting a personal mistake, the speaker shows the real cost of unclear code and makes the advice feel earned rather than preachy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By mentioning leaving the job, the speaker suggests that programmers should avoid changing employers too often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By admitting a personal mistake, the speaker shows the real cost of unclear code and makes the advice feel earned rather than preachy.$q$, $q$The speaker says the team lost "three weeks" because "I thought explanations were beneath me," taking the blame. The speech does not blame the other team; the point is that the speaker's own unclear code wasted their time.$q$, 'draft', '2be6111b-32d2-5cbc-9ffb-f2ed8c24afa7')
