  ('11ee09c3-eb8d-5fcc-b9bd-691853c184ed', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How do the sentences "None of this is glamorous. None of it will win a contest. All of it will decide whether your work survives." add to the speech's persuasiveness?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Two parallel concessions admit that clarity lacks prestige, and the shift from \"None\" to \"All\" makes the final claim land with extra force.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The three sentences admit that the advice is mostly unimportant, which shows the speaker wants listeners to focus on winning contests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"The three sentences summarize the anecdote that follows, which tells listeners in advance how the speaker's early program turned out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The three sentences list different coding languages, and the last one names the language most likely to survive in the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Two parallel concessions admit that clarity lacks prestige, and the shift from "None" to "All" makes the final claim land with extra force.$q$, $q$The repeated "None" grants the weaknesses of the advice, and the turn to "All" reverses them, stressing that clarity is what really matters. The concessions are a setup, not an admission that the advice is unimportant.$q$, 'draft', '2be6111b-32d2-5cbc-9ffb-f2ed8c24afa7')
