  ('ee95a2a7-cc8c-55db-b620-b7dd2c078e93', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the speaker discuss satellites and automated sensors in the fourth paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To suggest that Eleanor's notebooks should be replaced, by showing that modern machines make human observers unnecessary","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"To answer the likely objection that volunteers are no longer needed, by noting machines' short history and frequent changes","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain how satellites are built and launched, by describing the instruments they use to measure snow","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"To argue that satellites collect less data than volunteers, by comparing a single hour of machine data to Eleanor's notebooks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To answer the likely objection that volunteers are no longer needed, by noting machines' short history and frequent changes$q$, $q$The speaker grants that machines gather huge amounts of data, then notes they have "existed for only a fraction of the time" and get "replaced, upgraded, and moved." The speech says machines collect more data, not less, so the choice claiming satellites collect less data than volunteers reverses the speaker's words.$q$, 'draft', '81b91a97-1acd-5d90-9d86-ab6197b94f24')
