  ('05a8e563-f1ee-52b8-866a-b6115e0b667b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why does the speaker open by calling benches "the least exciting item in the downtown plan"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The understatement signals that the remarks will be short, since the speaker believes the topic does not deserve much of the committee's time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"The understatement criticizes the committee for focusing on exciting projects, which the speaker believes should all be cut from the plan.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The understatement reveals that the speaker personally finds benches boring and is presenting the request only as an assigned task.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The self-aware understatement disarms listeners' skepticism and frames the request as humble before the speaker argues for its importance.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The self-aware understatement disarms listeners' skepticism and frames the request as humble before the speaker argues for its importance.$q$, $q$By admitting up front that benches seem dull, the speaker anticipates the audience's reaction and then spends the speech showing why they matter. The firm request ("I am here to ask for sixty") shows the speaker does not find the topic unworthy.$q$, 'draft', '4b8fd98d-207e-59f4-8602-08897cb27068')
